class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: the published tree copy builds a scratch tree and copies it twice as cp -a does, each file into a temporary file renamed into place and each symbolic link made under a fresh name and renamed, keeping contents with their holes, permission bits and times and links as links, skipping a socket; the second copy replaces every entry of the first in one step, the listing reports links without following them, a read-only file refuses a write through a read-only descriptor and to an open for writing unless the process is root, a read past the end of a sparse file gives nothing, and a file with two names is two files in the copy
